Package: pord
Type: Package
Title: Exact Conditional Tests for Paired Ordinal Data on a Square Table
Version: 0.2.0
Date: 2026-08-19
Authors@R:
    person("Kenichi", "Satoh",
           email = "kenichi-satoh@biwako.shiga-u.ac.jp",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-4436-9347"))
Maintainer: Kenichi Satoh <kenichi-satoh@biwako.shiga-u.ac.jp>
URL: https://github.com/ksatohds/pord
BugReports: https://github.com/ksatohds/pord/issues
Description: Exact conditional tests for paired ordinal data recorded on the
    same K-point scale, such as expectation and achievement rated by the same
    respondent. The primary test asks whether the number of pairs with
    y >= x exceeds what independence would give, conditioning on both margins
    of the K x K table. This is a generalization of Fisher's exact test: it
    uses the same conditioning (the Fisher-Yates multiple hypergeometric
    distribution) and reduces to Fisher's exact test when the scale is
    dichotomized, but the test statistic counts one direction only. The null
    distribution is obtained exactly by dynamic programming, with permutation
    and closed-form normal approximations available as alternatives; the null
    mean and variance have closed forms depending only on the two margins.
    Companion functions provide the sign test for y < x, group comparison
    by label permutation, and diagnostics for how the margins govern power.
